.TH SDL_GetEventFilter 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetEventFilter \- Query the current event filter.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_events.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetEventFilter(SDL_EventFilter *filter, void **userdata);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function can be used to \(dqchain\(dq filters, by saving the existing filter before replacing it with a function that will call that saved filter\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I filter
the current callback function will be stored here\[char46]
.TP
.I userdata
the pointer that is passed to the current event filter will be stored here\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false if there is no event filter set\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_SetEventFilter (3)
